stranger things and kinda thought it would be something like that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1952-agent_m","name":"Agent_M","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T15:52:57-07:00","id":976772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/976443-hisil?p=976561#post976561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/78863-what-does-the-shadow-look-like?p=81134#post81134\">This</a> is my favorite explanation ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this, it definitely helps and I'm going to go through some of these other examples as these are great so far and helping. What about spirits though? How often do you encounter spirits? Is everything a spirit? Are they always hostile to you? I think I read that in the core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1952-agent_m","name":"Agent_M","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T18:52:00-07:00","id":976870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agent_M</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/976443-hisil?p=976772#post976772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this, it definitely helps and I'm going to go through some of these other examples as these are great so far and helping. What about spirits though? How often do you encounter spirits? Is everything a spirit? Are they always hostile to you? I think I read that in the core book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much everything is a spirit, yes. But not all of them are active; in fact, most are dormant. And most spirits are likely to be hostile towards werewolves in the same way that people in low-income neighborhoods are hostile towards cops. That is to say, they have a strained relationship, but that doesn't mean they're likely to start a confrontation for no reason. Tensions will be high, but most of the spirits you encounter aren't <i>looking</i> for a fight, they just expect that you are, and may be defensive as a result.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T03:04:16-07:00","id":977086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/976443-hisil?p=976870#post976870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And most spirits are likely to be hostile towards werewolves in the same way that people in low-income neighborhoods are hostile towards cops. That is to say, they have a strained relationship, but that doesn't mean they're likely to start a confrontation for no reason. Tensions will be high, but most of the spirits you encounter aren't <i>looking</i> for a fight, they just expect that you are, and may be defensive as a result.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting way to put it. I like it. So i've read in the hunting ground rockies book spirits are fighting for control over the city, do they group together and claim territory in the spirit realm like wolves do in the real one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1952-agent_m","name":"Agent_M","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T19:44:12-07:00","id":977538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/902501-a-grab-bag-of-shadow\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/902501-a-grab-bag-of-shadow\"> A grab-bag of Shadow - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/902501-a-grab-bag-of-shadow\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/902501-a-grab-bag-of-shadow </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> A lot of people have trouble visualising the Hisil, or coming up with ideas for how the Shadow representation of an area could appear. This is a thread to help fix that. (I don't recall a thread dealing with this before. If we have one, please point me towards it.) Here's the game - pick any place that you think is likely to be part of a territory and describe how it appears in the Hisil. Describe what it looks like, what spirits you find there, how they interact, and how they're likely to react to Uratha intruders. (This can be as broad or narrow as you like. A spirit ecology may respond well to </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Use this to picture the hisil in your mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T23:00:19-07:00","id":977617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agent_M</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/976443-hisil?p=977086#post977086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's an interesting way to put it. I like it. So i've read in the hunting ground rockies book spirits are fighting for control over the city, do they group together and claim territory in the spirit realm like wolves do in the real one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of. They compete over sources of Essence that match their Resonance, and spread their Influence. Weaker spirits flock around more powerful spirits with similar Influences, creating mini-spirit courts. You could say that where werewolves compete for physical territory, spirits compete for conceptual territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T04:43:07-07:00","id":977688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/976443-hisil?p=977617#post977617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of. They compete over sources of Essence that match their Resonance, and spread their Influence. Weaker spirits flock around more powerful spirits with similar Influences, creating mini-spirit courts. You could say that where werewolves compete for physical territory, spirits compete for conceptual territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK that makes some sense. I've been reading that other thread about random locals in the shadow with the stuff talked about here and I'm kind of getting a better grasp on it. So if a new pack moved into some fresh turf with a loci in it they would almost certainly be confronted with a spirit brood that is feeding from it right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1952-agent_m","name":"Agent_M","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T05:10:50-07:00","id":977695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agent_M</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/976443-hisil?p=977688#post977688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK that makes some sense. I've been reading that other thread about random locals in the shadow with the stuff talked about here and I'm kind of getting a better grasp on it. So if a new pack moved into some fresh turf with a loci in it they would almost certainly be confronted with a spirit brood that is feeding from it right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the size, age, and Resonance of said locus. It's possible for a small to mid-size locus to have one spirit that feeds on it exclusively, having eaten other competing spirits. It's unlikely a really powerful locus has nothing attached to it, I think, but you could come up with reasons for anything. Sometimes spirits go dormant or get killed or trapped. A totem that was once the sole resident of a locus' zone of influence may no longer need it. Werewolves perform sacred hunts, mages lock them up, 'wars' can leave areas vacant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T00:25:35-07:00","id":978253,"title":"","content":"Have we brought up magath yet? If not let's get into it. Spirits can eat spirits that aren't in line with their brood or prey, but it warps them terribly. An example would be a truck spirit towing cars that had consumed a snake spirit. A massive snake truck monster hunting cars along the spirit highway. <br /> <br /> If I remember correctly werewolves can succumb to this too on some level, but that may have just been first edition...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T02:37:11-07:00","id":978288,"title":"","content":"That was in the Spirit Predation section of the Forsaken Chronicler's Guide. Pretty neat stuff, and basically shoves the Sacred Hunt into being an even more core aspect of the game for First Edition. Looking at it now I'm thinking it makes more sense for the Sacred Hunt to be this core power rather than a Rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T05:50:21-07:00","id":978332,"title":"","content":"Magaths kinda confuse me still. These things werewolves seek to destroy everytime they find it right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1952-agent_m","name":"Agent_M","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T06:13:51-07:00","id":978336,"title":"","content":"Magath are abominations that spit in the face of what's normal. Even for the hisil. It'd be like finding a turtle with a rabbits head and an open maw of needles. <br /> <br /> And I think confusion is part of the idea really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T09:44:50-07:00","id":978451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agent_M</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/976443-hisil?p=978332#post978332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magaths kinda confuse me still. These things werewolves seek to destroy everytime they find it right?</div> </div> </div> </div>This was more the case in 1st edition.<br /> <br /> Basically, a Magath is a spirit that embodies multiple unrelated concepts. For example, Hunting Ground: the Rockies features a spirit of an Ice Cream Truck that consumed a spirit of predation, becoming a bizarre hybrid spirit of a predatory ice cream truck. With 1st edition's heavy focus on werewolves as inheritors of Father Wolf's sacred duty to maintain order between spirit and flesh, such a thing would have been seen as an abomination that transgresses the laws of the spirit world and must be destroyed. In 2e, the theme of inherited duty is still present, but it kind of takes a back seat to the theme of the sacred hunt. Magath are bizare and unnatural, yes, but different werewolves are going to respond to that differently. A Bone-Shadow, with their tribal Ban to pay each spirit in kind might want to put this poor creature out of its misery. A Hunter in Darkness, with their Ban to let no sacred place in their territory be violated would likely see a Magath in its territory as a violation, but might not care if it's beyond their borders. An Iron Master, who honor their territory in all things, might see a Magath in their territory as an important part of their territory's ecosystem and try to accommodate its presence, or they might see it as a threat to the humans in their territory and try to get rid of it.<br /> <br /> In the end, Magath are just spirits, and as with all spirits, different werewolves will deal with them in different ways. The thing to keep in mind is that they are spirits who's own natures contradict themselves, which means they merit special consideration as spirits that violate the normal order of the Hisil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T10:09:06-07:00","id":978461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agent_M</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/976443-hisil?p=978332#post978332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magaths kinda confuse me still. These things werewolves seek to destroy everytime they find it right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, magath was confusing to me at first, especially because there are certain spirit concepts that seem to naturally include two or more purviews that are already covered by separate spirit types: A murder spirit that seems like it should cover both death and fear, choirs of spirits like elemental &quot;artificial&quot; spirits (spirits of plastic, electricity, etc) or weather spirits (storm spirits as both water and air), and so on. The reason these things are not magath is because the hybrid resonances they feed on are &quot;naturally&quot; closely related, like the aforementioned murder spirit with influence over death and fear - obviously related concepts.<br /> <br /> A spirit is most clearly magath when it consistently feeds on two or more resonances with little to no overlap on a venn diagram, especially when those resonances cross over to other spirit types. A conceptual spirit of pain who begins to feed on Wind spirits and their resonances becomes an entirely unnatural amalgamation of the two types of spirit, disrupting the local hisil ecology like an invasive species, growing fat more quickly than is natural off it's increased resonance menu, and using it's influences to unbalance the flesh in a similarly dramatic way. Most importantly, because other spirits often hate and seek to destroy magath, they are the type of spirit that is especially likely to attempt to escape across the gauntlet and cause havoc in the flesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/358-emanantvolition","user":"EmanantVolition","date":". 09-29-2016, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/358-emanantvolition","name":"EmanantVolition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}